Measured (release, IO thread 30 ms, idle): the IO thread uses 74% of a core; one Poll = 85 ms = station states 84 ms (40 stations on the wire, ring 0 13 / ring 1 27, Acm_DevGetSlaveStates 2.1 ms each) + DI 0.3 + axes 0.75 + DO 0.15. Every 30 s one Poll took 1.26 s: ax14-18 (stations 35/36/38/39/40, not Yaskawa) kCfgGear + kCfgDrive fail every time, 29 SDO reads / ~252 ms per axis, all five on the same Poll -- no DI read meanwhile.

EtherCAT/Pci1203Monitor.cpp (6 lines, all same-line, no line moves): no try limit (was cfgTries < 3 on the 30 s window, every failed axis at once); a retry round opens every 60 s and retries ONE axis per Poll (Impl cfgRetryAxis / cfgRoundOn / cfgRoundNext / cfgRoundTick); on a pure retry (the group is not due for open / rescan / write, cfgDueNow) the gear group stops at its first failure and the drive group skips the rest after Pn21D fails. 603Fh retries, torque backoff (30 s window) and the station-state loop are unchanged.

Measured after: worst Poll 1350 ms -> ~110 ms (85 + one axis retry ~24 ms), no second-long Poll in 150 s. o2 full build 0 errors; ctest 382/400, failures = the known list; production_audit: every change was written before the measurement wb_serve closed at 14:27:16, 0 files after (ctest wrote nothing), baseline re-snapshotted; Debug then release wb_serve rebuilt. WORKLOG item 133.

